 "utterances": [
  {
   "start": 2.69,
   "end": 8.29,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Morning, everyone. You all there? Teams is showing me about three different versions of who's joined."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.09,
   "end": 13.64,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Yeah, I'm here. Yours froze for a second, but we can hear you."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.9,
   "end": 17.35,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Same here. Just getting the headset straight."
  },
  {
   "start": 19.54,
   "end": 25.84,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "I'm here, without coffee. The broken coffee machine in the canteen has really improved the atmosphere this morning."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.46,
   "end": 35.51,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Oh, the broken coffee machine in the canteen got me as well. Stood there pressing the button like it might change its mind."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.78,
   "end": 38.53,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Persistence. That's engineering, that is."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.03,
   "end": 43.48,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Depends how many times you pressed it."
  },
  {
   "start": 45.69,
   "end": 52.34,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Right, before we get the full fault history of that—Callum Reid's absent today. Let's have the updates first. Mide?"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.18,
   "end": 63.98,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Yeah, so, the training records for the new starters. I've had a first look through; nothing major so far. A fair bit of paperwork to get through, though."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.24,
   "end": 66.44,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Okay, thanks."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.11,
   "end": 71.66,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "Can I jump in? I've got mine and a quick one from Tommo."
  },
  {
   "start": 72.27,
   "end": 74.02,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Yep, go on, stores Jamie."
  },
  {
   "start": 74.74,
   "end": 82.79,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "I've made a start on the lock-out tag-out sign-off for the door switch on two. That's as far as I've got with it."
  },
  {
   "start": 85.28,
   "end": 94.38,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "And Tommo asked me to pass on that the guarding check on the stacker is all done. We weren't sure his headset was going to cooperate."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.3,
   "end": 98.8,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Cheers. Yeah, it picked a good moment to come back."
  },
  {
   "start": 99.73,
   "end": 106.73,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "The toolbox talk for the team is all organised now, from my side. No issues found with any of that."
  },
  {
   "start": 108.39,
   "end": 109.79,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Lovely, thanks, Fiona Doyle."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.27,
   "end": 116.17,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "And I've finished the filter swap on the power pack on one. That's sorted."
  },
  {
   "start": 116.89,
   "end": 123.19,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "While we're on filters, I already swapped the filter on the pump in the pit yesterday. All done."
  },
  {
   "start": 125.44,
   "end": 129.64,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "You looked like you'd been down a mine when you came back."
  },
  {
   "start": 130.99,
   "end": 133.09,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "It wasn't my finest look, no."
  },
  {
   "start": 134.48,
   "end": 136.93,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Doyler, was there anything else on yours?"
  },
  {
   "start": 139.34,
   "end": 147.74,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Yeah, the near-miss write-up for the arm on two—I'm not doing that now. The supplier's doing it under warranty instead, so ours is cancelled."
  },
  {
   "start": 148.08,
   "end": 149.28,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Right, understood."
  },
  {
   "start": 151.11,
   "end": 153.21,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "That's everything from the earlier stuff."
  },
  {
   "start": 154.69,
   "end": 162.74,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "Just an observation from me: I saw the pressure on the CT1 dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own."
  },
  {
   "start": 164.01,
   "end": 165.41,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Without anyone touching anything?"
  },
  {
   "start": 166.35,
   "end": 170.9,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "Yeah, no intervention. Back where it was. Just mentioning what I saw, really."
  },
  {
   "start": 171.48,
   "end": 173.58,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Mm, okay. A brief dip, then."
  },
  {
   "start": 174.28,
   "end": 175.68,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Thanks. Right, new work—Haley?"
  },
  {
   "start": 176.56,
   "end": 182.51,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the gas valve on one by the end of the week."
  },
  {
   "start": 184.84,
   "end": 189.39,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Okay, Haley, agreed. The seals on the gas valve on one are yours."
  },
  {
   "start": 191.82,
   "end": 193.22,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Yep, I'll take that."
  },
  {
   "start": 194.52,
   "end": 199.07,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Always sounds like a tiny job when you just say 'seals', doesn't it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 201.33,
   "end": 204.48,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Yeah, well, I'm not saying it's a five-minute one."
  },
  {
   "start": 204.83,
   "end": 207.28,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "End of the week, then. Got that."
  },
  {
   "start": 208.97,
   "end": 211.07,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Good. What else have we got?"
  },
  {
   "start": 213.07,
   "end": 219.02,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "I'll do a site visit at the hydraulics lot with the contractor tomorrow. Low priority, that one."
  },
  {
   "start": 219.69,
   "end": 221.44,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Yep, Aisha, agreed. Low priority."
  },
  {
   "start": 223.52,
   "end": 227.02,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Yeah. A visit with them, that's all I'm putting forward."
  },
  {
   "start": 227.34,
   "end": 231.54,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Tomorrow, Thursday. Sorry, my head was still on Tuesday for a moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.97,
   "end": 237.47,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Definitely tomorrow. This week's doing that to me as well."
  },
  {
   "start": 239.3,
   "end": 243.15,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Right, Aisha has the hydraulics lot visit with the contractor tomorrow."
  },
  {
   "start": 244.14,
   "end": 248.69,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "Sorry, was that me dropping out or did everyone get the robot voice?"
  },
  {
   "start": 250.77,
   "end": 253.22,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "Just you, I think. Sounded normal here."
  },
  {
   "start": 255.51,
   "end": 256.91,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "Ah, okay. Back now."
  },
  {
   "start": 258.25,
   "end": 260.35,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "Anything else new that needs agreeing?"
  },
  {
   "start": 261.08,
   "end": 262.48,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Nothing else from me."
  },
  {
   "start": 263.85,
   "end": 265.05,
   "speaker_id": "p10",
   "speaker": "Olumide Adeyemi",
   "text": "No, that's me."
  },
  {
   "start": 265.74,
   "end": 266.94,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Nothing further here."
  },
  {
   "start": 267.8,
   "end": 269.0,
   "speaker_id": "p08",
   "speaker": "Marcus Hale",
   "text": "Nope, all covered."
  },
  {
   "start": 271.06,
   "end": 274.56,
   "speaker_id": "p12",
   "speaker": "Jamie Brennan",
   "text": "Only my coffee grievance, and that's not a maintenance request."
  },
  {
   "start": 276.14,
   "end": 279.29,
   "speaker_id": "p07",
   "speaker": "Aisha Begum",
   "text": "Good, because I think we've given it enough airtime."
  },
  {
   "start": 279.59,
   "end": 282.04,
   "speaker_id": "p01",
   "speaker": "Sarah Okafor",
   "text": "We have. Right, thanks everyone. That's us."
  },
  {
   "start": 284.2,
   "end": 285.4,
   "speaker_id": "p09",
   "speaker": "Fiona Doyle",
   "text": "Cheers, all."
  },
  {
   "start": 287.27,
   "end": 288.47,
   "speaker_id": "p04",
   "speaker": "Tomasz Nowak",
   "text": "Cheers."
  }
 ],
